 "definition": "Gaze v2 memory contrast: scripts/gaze_memory.py's test, rerun under each instrument from gaze_v2_extract.py.\n\nPer speaker video (analysis/gaze_v2/<dyad>__<PID>.npz, 3 fps, own camera at 640x480, transcript time):\n  mp      : MediaPipe at full resolution, the ORIGINAL away rule: no face, or |head yaw - call median| > 15, or\n            |head pitch - median| > 15, or max eye-look blendshape (out/up/down) - median > 0.3.\n  mp_head : MediaPipe head pose only (no face, or yaw/pitch > 15 deg from median); the backstop for downward gaze.\n  ug_T    : UniGaze (camera-space gaze): no usable normalized face, or |gaze yaw - median| > T, or |gaze pitch - median| > T.\n  pg_T    : PureGaze (ETH-XGaze), same rule.            T in {10, 15, 20}; 15 is primary (fixed before looking at labels).\n  both_15 : away only when UniGaze AND PureGaze both say away at 15 (no face counts for both).\nRememberer = the reporter (their own camera); partner = the other speaker's OWN camera (v1 used the partner's stream as\nreceived on the rememberer's machine, inside the 320x240 composite).\nPer turn [start, next start): each person's away rate, centered within the call. Contrasts exactly as gaze_memory.py:\ninside the located remembered stretch minus outside, position-matched (same fifth) or position x length-matched,\nby who is speaking; person-clustered bootstrap over rememberers (2,000).\nAgreement: frame-level correlation of UniGaze vs PureGaze gaze angles (centered per video), Cohen's kappa between the\naway flags of each instrument pair. -> analysis/gaze_memory_v2.json",
